LC 424 — Longest Repeating Character Replacement
Pattern:Sliding Window + Hashing

Logic:
Keep a window.
Find the most frequent character in the window.
Change the other characters to it.
If changes needed > k, shrink the window.
Keep maximum window length.

Algorithm:
maxFreq = most frequent character

window length - maxFreq = replacements needed

If replacements > k:
    move left pointer

Keep maximum length

CODE:
lass Solution {
public:
    int characterReplacement(string s, int k) {
        int count[26] = {};
        int i = 0, maxFreq = 0, ans = 0;

        for (int j = 0; j < s.size(); j++) {
            count[s[j] - 'A']++;
            maxFreq = max(maxFreq, count[s[j] - 'A']);

            while (j - i + 1 - maxFreq > k) {
                count[s[i] - 'A']--;
                i++;
            }

            ans = max(ans, j - i + 1);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};

s = "AABABBA"
k = 1

